   "notes": [
    "TDC quantization follows the modulation: 0.09 TDC bins of RMS dither, under 0.5.  The modulation sweeps the TDC across bins deterministically, so the quantization error repeats with it from one modulation period to the next.  Its PSD level can still agree with analyze(); what fails is the randomness: averaging or coherently integrating over periods does not reduce it (measured on a 12.2 ps TDC, 1 ps jitter, 0.08 bin: the part common to all ramps 3-8 dB below the total at 0.3-10 MHz, against 12 dB for random noise over 16 ramps).  TDCConfig.dither_lsb breaks it up without adding noise (2 LSB or more clears this note); more TDC jitter does too, at the cost of in-band noise.",
    "jitter integrated to 45 MHz (0.45x the reference-edge record rate), not the full 50 MHz band the linear model integrates \u2014 compare the two only over the common band"
   ],
