   "notes": [
    "TDC dead zone: integer-N (FCW 150) with 0.09 TDC bins of RMS dither at its input, under 0.5.  The loop parks inside one bin and cannot see the DCO drift there, so tdc_quant's white t_res^2/12 is not supported: simulate() can read up to ~20 dB more below the loop bandwidth (measured +16.9 dB at 0.08 bin, but +0.3 dB for the stock loop at 0.20 bin -- the size depends on the loop, so compare with simulate()).  A frequency ramp moves the TDC across bins but does not dither it: under 0.5 bin the quantization error then repeats with the ramp, which simulate() notes.  Not applicable in fractional-N.  TDC jitter of ~0.5 bin or more dithers the TDC, and so does TDCConfig.dither_lsb (subtractive, adds no noise): its RMS counts in the figure above, 0.29 bin per LSB, so 2 LSB or more clears this note.  1 LSB is not enough when a DCO period is not a whole number of codes (measured +2.4..+2.9 dB at 5.46 codes per period, 3 LSB within 0.8 dB)."
